  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of social stabilization and acceleration of economic recovery in Nineveh Governorate in Iraq</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to reviving the local economy of the Nineveh Governorate and to improving employability of conflict-affected people and communities, in particular internally displaced persons (IDPs) and returnees.  At the individual and household level, the project seeks to revitalize micro- and small enterprises that were operational before the conflict, assist the establishment of new income-generating activities, and provide untrained youth with technical skills. In addition, the upgrading of vocational training centers and national institutions ensures long/term institutional capacity-building contributing to the overall resettlement and stablization of the local economy.</narrative>
  </description>
